## Original Content
New 50% Trump administration tariffs on some Canadian exports went into place after the U.S. and Canada failed to reach a deal on Friday.

## Summary
U.S.-Canada trade talks collapsed on Friday after the two countries failed to reach a deal, triggering new 50% tariffs from the Trump administration on some Canadian exports. In response, Carney announced that Canada's retaliatory tariffs will take effect on September 8.

## Key Points
- U.S.-Canada trade negotiations failed to produce an agreement by Friday
- New 50% tariffs imposed by the Trump administration went into effect on certain Canadian exports
- Carney announced that Canadian retaliatory tariffs will begin on September 8


